fix: disambiguate slugs for split PS rows (primaria vs secundaria)

Two game rows that share the same (titulo, plataforma) - e.g. EA SPORTS
FC 26 "Primaria PS5" vs "Secundaria PS5" - collapsed to the same slug
(ea-sports-fc-26-ps5), so get_game_by_slug always returned the first
match, sending Secundaria clicks to the Primaria page.

The split rows each have exactly one active sellable modality. Use that
to extend the slug (e.g. ea-sports-fc-26-secundaria-ps5). Old bundled
rows (multiple modalities in one row) still get the legacy slug, and
get_game_by_slug keeps a legacy fallback so existing shared URLs
continue to resolve.

- backend/database.py: new generate_game_slug(game) + _active_modalities
- backend/server.py: use generate_game_slug when emitting URLs
- ui/juegos.html: mirror the same logic client-side so catalog cards
  link to the right page
